card.statement:
Given any tableau $T(L)$ of type $C$, we define the $C$-weight of $T(L)$ as $\omega(T(L))=(\omega_1(L),\omega_2(L),\ldots,\omega_n(L))$, where

\begin{align}
\omega_k(L):=2\sum_{i=1}^{k}\ell'_{ki}-\sum_{i=1}^{k}\ell_{ki}-\sum_{i=1}^{k-1}\ell_{k-1,i}+k-\frac{1}{2}.
\end{align}

In particular, the $C$-weight of $T(L)$ in $\mathcal B (\mat{\mu}, \mat{\lambda})$ is its $\mathfrak 
 h$-weight written as an element of $\mathbb C^n$.
